# Extra advisory lists for aur-cooldown (optional).
#
# aur-cooldown already consumes a campaign denylist by default: the
# community-maintained aur-malware-check campaigns.json, which carries a date
# window per campaign. Versions pushed inside a campaign's window are refused;
# clean versions outside it are not. You do NOT need to configure that here, and
# you can turn it off or repoint it with the `denylist` / `denylist_source` keys
# in the config file (see config.example).
#
# This file is only for ADDITIONAL lists you trust. Copy it to
# ~/.config/aur-cooldown/denylist-feeds and add one URL per line. Each URL must
# return plain text, one AUR package name per line, '#' comments allowed.
#
# These extra lists have no date window, so aur-cooldown treats them as an
# ADVISORY: if an installed package is listed, it is reported (with a suggestion
# to hard-block via IgnorePkg) but not auto-frozen, because a bare name can't be
# scoped to a specific bad version. Lists are fetched by `observe` and
# `refresh`; on fetch failure the previous cache is kept.
#
#https://example.org/my-trusted-aur-blocklist.txt
